[thin] Required First Edition graphic outlines: the identification strokes, frame, divider and QR modules follow the artwork master and the plate's shared scale. The zero-area sample is a narrowing at a glyph curve junction. These points belong to the raised lettering, QR and frame. The resized artwork has Derek's visual approval; its physical print is unqualified.
alternatives: Heavier glyphs or larger lettering change the approved type or its balanced layout. A wider frame changes the requested fine border. Larger QR modules increase its footprint; flush ink removes the required relief. Use a variable-width print process for the scaled identification strokes.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/nameplate/nameplate-001.step
